From 75616b9307c1be0edd0223fb23dbf4192b2222c8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alexis Williams <alexis@typedr.at>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 14:36:59 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 20/20] spa: alsa: Follow external volume changes via Monitor

ACP opens a second connection for the streaming Monitor call and
applies the pushed volume and mute to the active route, so changes
made on the device itself show up in PipeWire.

If the service is unreachable when the card comes up, or goes away
later, both connections are retried on a timer, starting at 1 s and
backing off to 30 s. The main connection and Monitor back off
separately, so a service that keeps refusing Monitor doesn't delay
reconnecting the main connection. Losing the service is logged once,
retries quietly, and recovery once.

A replacement connection is swapped in only once it works, so calls
fail meanwhile instead of falling through to the card's own mixer.
Capabilities learned on a late connect install the devices' volume
and mute hooks then and drop any software volume applied before. A
Monitor stream that ends is restarted.

Volume and mute changes also publish the device's updated routes
right away. Mixer changes get that from the poll handler, but service
updates arrive on their own socket, and mixers read the route.
